WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.050 --> 00:00:05.170
WandaVision is one hell of a weird show and
whether you love it or are just plain confused,

00:00:05.170 --> 00:00:08.600
you'll want to know how it connects with the
rest of the MCU.

00:00:08.600 --> 00:00:12.800
And like any great mystery, there are a ton
of clues that reveal the show's connections

00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:15.320
to the Avengers, Spider-Man and even the X-Men.

00:00:15.320 --> 00:00:19.650
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, I'm Jan and in
this video I'm explaining the weirdest and

00:00:19.650 --> 00:00:24.710
most perplexing scenes, theories, MCU references
and easter eggs in WandaVision.

00:00:24.710 --> 00:00:28.369
Plus I'll explain the new Phase 4 villains
like Mephisto and Grim Reaper that we can

00:00:28.369 --> 00:00:30.029
expect to see in the show.

00:00:30.029 --> 00:00:33.340
Spoilers and speculation ahead, of course!

00:00:33.340 --> 00:00:38.770
Set in Westview, WandaVision takes places
in a strange new sitcom reality that Wanda

00:00:38.770 --> 00:00:40.489
appears to have created for herself.

00:00:40.489 --> 00:00:45.109
A clue that Wanda and Vision are living inside
their own bubble reality or pocket dimension

00:00:45.109 --> 00:00:49.800
is the curious design of Vision's tie with
two dots inside a rectangle with two more

00:00:49.800 --> 00:00:51.680
dots on the outside.

00:00:51.680 --> 00:00:56.010
And given the SWORD encampment that's been
set up in this wooded area and a strange energy

00:00:56.010 --> 00:01:00.859
field nearby, it suggests that Wanda may have
taken over a town with her powers.

00:01:00.859 --> 00:01:06.470
This would explain why the real world occasionally
seems to leak into Wanda's alternate reality,

00:01:06.470 --> 00:01:09.080
such as when a voice on the radio calls out
to Wanda.

00:01:09.080 --> 00:01:10.080
"Wanda.

00:01:10.080 --> 00:01:11.320
Who's doing this to you Wanda?"

00:01:11.320 --> 00:01:12.910
And when Dottie asks who she really is.

00:01:12.910 --> 00:01:13.910
"Who are you?"

00:01:13.910 --> 00:01:19.460
A similar moment happens when Mr Hart is choking
at the dinner table, and his wife tells him

00:01:19.460 --> 00:01:24.320
over and over to "stop it", although this
instruction seems to be almost directed towards

00:01:24.320 --> 00:01:25.540
Wanda instead.

00:01:25.540 --> 00:01:27.050
"Stop it.

00:01:27.050 --> 00:01:28.560
Stop it.

00:01:28.560 --> 00:01:30.070
Stop it."

00:01:30.070 --> 00:01:34.700
It's a very weird and creepy moment especially
as after Vision uses his phasing ability to

00:01:34.700 --> 00:01:39.130
pull out the food, everyone seems to forget
that anything happened and they leave.

00:01:39.130 --> 00:01:44.320
I think that Wanda may be using her reality-bending
or illusion-inducing powers that we saw her

00:01:44.320 --> 00:01:49.250
use in Age of Ultron against the Avengers
to maintain the idealised world she's created

00:01:49.250 --> 00:01:50.710
for herself in Westview.

00:01:50.710 --> 00:01:55.210
It appears that characters can actually get
hurt though, such as when Dottie cuts her

00:01:55.210 --> 00:01:57.610
hand and we can see the blood in actual colour.

00:01:57.610 --> 00:02:02.560
By the way, the voice on the radio sounds
a lot like Randall Park, aka Jimmy Woo from

00:02:02.560 --> 00:02:06.560
Ant-Man and the Wasp, who we know is now working
for SWORD in WandaVision.

00:02:06.560 --> 00:02:11.311
SWORD is the acronym for the "Sentient Weapon
Observation and Response Division" and you

00:02:11.311 --> 00:02:15.010
can see they're the ones monitoring Wanda
and Vision at the end of the first episode.

00:02:15.010 --> 00:02:20.260
It also suggests that the agency views Wanda
and or Vision to be sentient weapons that

00:02:20.260 --> 00:02:22.430
could pose a threat.

00:02:22.430 --> 00:02:27.440
There's also a deep-cut easter egg in this
scene referencing the wider MCU multiverse,

00:02:27.440 --> 00:02:31.370
when the fake credits for the WandaVision
show roll by and we see that the name of the

00:02:31.370 --> 00:02:34.830
director is "Abe Brown", one of Peter Parker's
classmates.

00:02:34.830 --> 00:02:38.440
Abe was a Spider-Man character who survived
the Snap, and this suggests that he's now

00:02:38.440 --> 00:02:40.200
working for SWORD.

00:02:40.200 --> 00:02:44.640
And it might even point to Wanda appearing
in the next MCU Spider-Man movie, given we

00:02:44.640 --> 00:02:47.740
know that she's already in Doctor Strange
and the Multiverse of Madness

00:02:47.740 --> 00:02:51.800
especially since Spider-Man 3 will be featuring
the Spider-Man multiverse with appearances

00:02:51.800 --> 00:02:55.180
from Alfred Molina's Doc Oc and Jamie Foxx's
Electro.

00:02:55.180 --> 00:02:59.490
There's evidently a lot more to Wanda's nosy
neighbour than she's letting on.

00:02:59.490 --> 00:03:03.860
And given we see her dressed as a witch later
in the series, many fans are assuming she's

00:03:03.860 --> 00:03:08.650
playing the comic book character Agatha Harkness,
a witch from Salem, especially as her name

00:03:08.650 --> 00:03:11.980
Agness combines the first and last syllables
of "Agatha Harkness".

00:03:11.980 --> 00:03:17.220
However, I think this may be almost too obvious
and Marvel is planning a little twist and

00:03:17.220 --> 00:03:21.250
she turns out to be Mephisto, one of Phase
4's next big villains.

00:03:21.250 --> 00:03:24.000
One of the clues is in how she reacts to Dottie
in this scene.

00:03:24.000 --> 00:03:25.770
"The devil's in the details, Bev."

00:03:25.770 --> 00:03:27.740
"That's not the only place he is."

00:03:27.740 --> 00:03:32.380
And then she has a pet rabbit called "Señor
Scratchy" which is a big clue because "Mr

00:03:32.380 --> 00:03:34.510
Scratch" is a nickname for the devil.

00:03:34.510 --> 00:03:38.770
This might also be a reference to Agness's
son in the comics, Nicholas Scratch, a major

00:03:38.770 --> 00:03:40.950
Fantastic Four supervillain.

00:03:40.950 --> 00:03:46.010
Agness even draws attention to Scratch's importance
"Señor Scratchy just loves the stage.

00:03:46.010 --> 00:03:49.709
He played baby Jesus in last year's Christmas
pageant."

00:03:49.709 --> 00:03:54.819
For those unfamiliar, Mephisto is an extremely
powerful demonic villain who rules a pocket

00:03:54.819 --> 00:03:58.850
dimension called Hell in the comics,
and who seems set to become an important villain

00:03:58.850 --> 00:04:04.060
in the MCU given the prominent display of
a devil in a stained glass window in the Loki

00:04:04.060 --> 00:04:05.060
trailer.

00:04:05.060 --> 00:04:08.830
It's also interesting that Agness constantly
jokes in the show about her husband Ralph,

00:04:08.830 --> 00:04:10.630
who we mysteriously haven't seen yet.

00:04:10.630 --> 00:04:15.380
"The only way Ralph would remember our anniversary
is if there was a beer named June 2nd."

00:04:15.380 --> 00:04:19.779
The name Ralph is significant because he's
a character from Christopher Marlowe's play

00:04:19.779 --> 00:04:24.350
Doctor Faustus who helped conjure devils such
as Mephistopheles, who the Marvel villain

00:04:24.350 --> 00:04:27.530
Mephisto is based on and named after.

00:04:27.530 --> 00:04:31.360
Another mystery in the show is the identity
of the beekeeper who climbs out of a sewer

00:04:31.360 --> 00:04:32.819
at the end of the second episode.

00:04:32.819 --> 00:04:37.860
A clue from a new featurette shows that this
appears to be a SWORD agent being sent into

00:04:37.860 --> 00:04:40.229
the pocket dimension that Wanda and Vision
are in,

00:04:40.229 --> 00:04:45.039
as you can see him crawling through a tunnel
and then his hazmat suit changes into a beekeeper's

00:04:45.039 --> 00:04:46.039
costume.

00:04:46.039 --> 00:04:47.169
Why a beekeeper though?

00:04:47.169 --> 00:04:51.389
Well, although it may be a reference to the
Marvel supervillain Swarm whose body is made

00:04:51.389 --> 00:04:56.439
up of bees, bees themselves actually have
some specific symbolism that's very appropriate

00:04:56.439 --> 00:04:57.610
to WandaVision.

00:04:57.610 --> 00:05:02.550
As pollinators, they're frequently associated
with fertility and reproduction, and so link

00:05:02.550 --> 00:05:04.069
to Wanda's pregnancy.

00:05:04.069 --> 00:05:08.439
And in Celtic mythology, bees are regarded
as messengers between heaven and earth or

00:05:08.439 --> 00:05:11.409
different realms
which is also fitting because the beekeeper's

00:05:11.409 --> 00:05:16.199
arrival seems to be an attempt from the world
outside to make contact with Wanda.

00:05:16.199 --> 00:05:22.240
Wanda either consciously or intuitively understands
this and when she sees him she says "No" and

00:05:22.240 --> 00:05:26.569
rewinds time back to the moment when she asks
Vision if "this is really happening";

00:05:26.569 --> 00:05:31.460
and this time rather than going outside, she
transforms their world into a now colour-filled

00:05:31.460 --> 00:05:33.449
sitcom reality.

00:05:33.449 --> 00:05:36.189
Wanda being able to rewind time here for a
do-over,

00:05:36.189 --> 00:05:41.430
reminds me of how Vision died twice in Infinity
War when Thanos rewound time to undo Wanda's

00:05:41.430 --> 00:05:46.129
destruction of the Mind Stone, so that he
could take the infinity stone for himself.

00:05:46.129 --> 00:05:49.159
More on Wanda's time manipulation powers shortly.

00:05:49.159 --> 00:05:53.340
The "No" that Wanda says to the Beekeeper
may also be a reference to Wanda's famous

00:05:53.340 --> 00:05:58.229
line "No more mutants" from the "House of
'M'" storyline, in which Scarlet Witch caused

00:05:58.229 --> 00:06:01.210
almost every mutant to lose their powers.

00:06:01.210 --> 00:06:05.770
Marvel Studios might be looking to subvert
this iconic comic book moment by having Wanda

00:06:05.770 --> 00:06:11.249
be the gateway to bringing mutants and the
X-Men into the MCU, so look out for her saying

00:06:11.249 --> 00:06:13.659
"more mutants" later on in the series.

00:06:13.659 --> 00:06:17.639
And there's another neat reference to the
"House of 'M'" via the wine served at Wanda's

00:06:17.639 --> 00:06:18.639
dinner party.

00:06:18.639 --> 00:06:23.559
The bottle's label reads "Maison du Mépris"
which translates to English as "House of Contempt",

00:06:23.559 --> 00:06:26.490
plus there's a letter 'M' around the neck
of the bottle.

00:06:26.490 --> 00:06:31.259
And WandaVision's credits are a cool visual
nod to the way her mental breakdown in the

00:06:31.259 --> 00:06:35.509
comics is represented by her disintegrating
reality into blocks.

00:06:35.509 --> 00:06:40.599
There are some especially creepy moments in
the second episode when the various residents

00:06:40.599 --> 00:06:45.159
of Westview chant "For the children" together:
"For the children.

00:06:45.159 --> 00:06:46.610
For the children.

00:06:46.610 --> 00:06:48.069
For the children."

00:06:48.069 --> 00:06:52.619
Then there's Mrs Hart who badgers Wanda and
Vision about why they don't have children

00:06:52.619 --> 00:06:57.120
and the headline on the newspaper that Vision
reads says "Little Baby June's First Words

00:06:57.120 --> 00:06:58.889
Tickle Mother Sue".

00:06:58.889 --> 00:07:03.659
Agnes also seems to be very keen on getting
Wanda to seduce Vision in the first episode.

00:07:03.659 --> 00:07:05.669
"What about seduction techniques?"

00:07:05.669 --> 00:07:10.360
And Dottie is another mysterious character
intent on pushing the "For the children" agenda.

00:07:10.360 --> 00:07:14.059
On top of that, it's particularly disturbing
that there aren't even any children around

00:07:14.059 --> 00:07:15.309
in these scenes.

00:07:15.309 --> 00:07:19.789
However, all of these pressures seem to have
worked into brainwashing the couple by the

00:07:19.789 --> 00:07:21.229
end of episode two.

00:07:21.229 --> 00:07:24.029
"And it was all for the children."

00:07:24.029 --> 00:07:28.360
And just like that, as if by magic, Wanda
discovers she's pregnant, perhaps because

00:07:28.360 --> 00:07:30.180
she simply decided it.

00:07:30.180 --> 00:07:34.509
It feels like there's some strange presence
at work here, lurking in the background, such

00:07:34.509 --> 00:07:39.409
as Mephisto, who could be looking to take
control of Wanda's children who will undoubtedly

00:07:39.409 --> 00:07:41.439
be super-powered when they're born.

00:07:41.439 --> 00:07:45.370
In the comics, when Wanda has children, she
discovers they're the outcome of her magic

00:07:45.370 --> 00:07:47.929
mixing with fragments of Mephisto's soul.

00:07:47.929 --> 00:07:52.410
Now, the MCU won't be following the comic
book storylines exactly, however, it often

00:07:52.410 --> 00:07:56.809
takes elements and inspiration from them,
so it's quite likely that Mephisto has something

00:07:56.809 --> 00:07:59.509
to do with Wanda's pregnancy and children.

00:07:59.509 --> 00:08:03.569
It's also possible that Wanda made a bargain
with the devil to bring Vision back to life

00:08:03.569 --> 00:08:07.449
and he'll later try to collect on the deal
by taking away her children.

00:08:07.449 --> 00:08:11.399
Is that what the voice means when it asks
Wanda, "Who is doing this to you?"

00:08:11.399 --> 00:08:15.770
The fake ad breaks also provide some more
clues as to what may be going on in Wanda's

00:08:15.770 --> 00:08:20.729
mind and how she may be processing the various
traumas she's experienced in her life.

00:08:20.729 --> 00:08:25.139
The watch commercial advertising Strucker
watches is, of course, a reference to Baron

00:08:25.139 --> 00:08:29.929
von Strucker, the HYDRA leader who experimented
on Wanda and her brother Pietro with the Mind

00:08:29.929 --> 00:08:30.929
Stone.

00:08:30.929 --> 00:08:31.929
"Strücker.

00:08:31.929 --> 00:08:33.839
He'll make time for you."

00:08:33.839 --> 00:08:38.630
But this is more than just an easter egg for
Marvel fans, as I think it's implying that

00:08:38.630 --> 00:08:42.849
Wanda may have inherited more powers than
we realise from the Mind Stone,

00:08:42.849 --> 00:08:47.990
including the ability to manipulate and rewind
time, which she did after seeing the Beekeeper.

00:08:47.990 --> 00:08:52.040
And there was another awesome HYDRA easter
egg, cleverly hidden on the wallpaper in Wanda's

00:08:52.040 --> 00:08:53.040
home.

00:08:53.040 --> 00:08:57.010
As she turns everything to colour, you can
see the Sokovian HYDRA Research Base where

00:08:57.010 --> 00:09:00.690
Wanda and her brother were kept and which
the Avengers attacked at the beginning of

00:09:00.690 --> 00:09:01.690
Age of Ultron.

00:09:01.690 --> 00:09:06.399
Again, this is Wanda's way of processing this
particular trauma.

00:09:06.399 --> 00:09:12.100
The ad for a ToastMate 2000 by Stark Industries
is another traumatic reference for Wanda because

00:09:12.100 --> 00:09:17.380
remember that she had an intense hatred for
Stark after one of his bombs killed her parents.

00:09:17.380 --> 00:09:21.550
And listen very carefully during the commercial
because the noise that the toaster makes is

00:09:21.550 --> 00:09:27.529
the same sound effect that Iron Man's blaster
makes as it powers up.

00:09:27.529 --> 00:09:31.670
And the uncomfortable look on the housewife's
face as she waits for the bread to toast may

00:09:31.670 --> 00:09:36.730
be a nod to how Wanda and Pietro spent two
days staring at Stark's bomb waiting for it

00:09:36.730 --> 00:09:37.730
go to go off.

00:09:37.730 --> 00:09:39.000
"We wait for two days.

00:09:39.000 --> 00:09:41.230
For Tony Stark to kill us."

00:09:41.230 --> 00:09:45.740
The message at the end of the ad, "Forget
the past, this is your future!", seems to

00:09:45.740 --> 00:09:50.120
indicate that Wanda is trying to suppress
her painful memories and traumas through this

00:09:50.120 --> 00:09:51.880
new reality she's created.

00:09:51.880 --> 00:09:56.510
If you're wondering where Monica Rambeau is
in WandaVision, well she's already appeared

00:09:56.510 --> 00:09:59.339
on the show, but her character is currently
called Geraldine.

00:09:59.339 --> 00:10:00.339
"I'm Wanda."

00:10:00.339 --> 00:10:01.339
"I'm, uh...

00:10:01.339 --> 00:10:02.339
Geraldine.

00:10:02.339 --> 00:10:05.100
I actually don't know what I'm doing here."

00:10:05.100 --> 00:10:09.080
The loud crash that Wanda and Vision hear
at night at the beginning of the second episode

00:10:09.080 --> 00:10:13.240
is a SWORD helicopter that I think Monica
Rambeau was piloting but which crashed through

00:10:13.240 --> 00:10:15.120
to Westview from the world outside.

00:10:15.120 --> 00:10:19.829
And it's represented by the red toy helicopter
that Wanda picks up the next day with a SWORD

00:10:19.829 --> 00:10:20.829
logo on it.

00:10:20.829 --> 00:10:24.300
There's a clever reference to this in the
magic trick that Vision and Wanda perform

00:10:24.300 --> 00:10:29.620
later that day when Geraldine is teleported
from behind the stage into the Cabinet of

00:10:29.620 --> 00:10:30.620
Mysteries.

00:10:30.620 --> 00:10:34.509
And by the way, a cool detail here on the
cabinet artwork is the Mind Stone which looks

00:10:34.509 --> 00:10:39.399
like it could be exploding, referencing how
Wanda destroyed the Stone in Vision's forehead

00:10:39.399 --> 00:10:40.529
in Infinity War.

00:10:40.529 --> 00:10:44.930
Again this may be another way that Wanda is
processing another traumatic event from her

00:10:44.930 --> 00:10:46.080
life.

00:10:46.080 --> 00:10:52.470
I also think it's interesting that Vision
refers to himself as an illusion in this scene,

00:10:52.470 --> 00:10:56.690
a possible bit of foreshadowing that this
version of Vision may not be who he seems

00:10:56.690 --> 00:10:57.690
to be.

00:10:57.690 --> 00:10:58.690
"Of course I did the trick right!

00:10:58.690 --> 00:10:59.690
I'm Illusion!"

00:10:59.690 --> 00:11:02.910
In fact, in a recent trailer, I noticed Wanda
and Vision are facing off against each other,

00:11:02.910 --> 00:11:07.360
so could Vision himself even turn out to be
the villain of WandaVision?

00:11:07.360 --> 00:11:12.080
He is dead after all in the real world, so
could this Vision actually be a villain like

00:11:12.080 --> 00:11:14.260
Mephisto in disguise?

00:11:14.260 --> 00:11:19.009
And as Illusion's magic assistant, Wanda is
called Glamour, perhaps hinting that a glamour

00:11:19.009 --> 00:11:23.480
or spell has been cast on her or Vision to
hide whatever is really going on.

00:11:23.480 --> 00:11:28.860
And this might be a stretch, but the way that
each episode ends with Wanda and Vision enclosed

00:11:28.860 --> 00:11:32.440
in a hexagon might also be suggesting that
a hex has been put on her.

00:11:32.440 --> 00:11:35.730
A hex being an evil spell that brings bad
luck and trouble.

00:11:35.730 --> 00:11:41.379
On top of that, a hexagon is also six-sided,
a hint perhaps to the devil's number 666,

00:11:41.379 --> 00:11:44.550
together with the fact that this radio is
strangely missing a six.

00:11:44.550 --> 00:11:49.810
And, of course, honeycombs are also often
made up of hexagonal formations, a potential

00:11:49.810 --> 00:11:52.129
reference to the mysterious bee keeper then.

00:11:52.129 --> 00:11:56.940
A few other easter eggs you might have missed
which may be significant include the Grim

00:11:56.940 --> 00:11:59.850
Reaper's helmet in the second episode's opening
credits.

00:11:59.850 --> 00:12:04.399
The Grim Reaper is a Marvel comics villain
and is rumoured to be appearing in WandaVision.

00:12:04.399 --> 00:12:08.560
Plus, there's a possible easter egg to Wonder
Man, Grim Reaper's brother, in the credits

00:12:08.560 --> 00:12:09.560
here.

00:12:09.560 --> 00:12:11.579
So, what do you think of WandaVision?

00:12:11.579 --> 00:12:13.519
And what are your favourite theories about
the show?

00:12:13.519 --> 00:12:15.759
Leave your thoughts in the comments below!

00:12:15.759 --> 00:12:19.089
And if you enjoyed this, leave a-thumbs up,
I really appreciate it.

00:12:19.089 --> 00:12:24.279
Tap left for my next Marvel video and my theory
about Black Widow's secret twist, or tap right

00:12:24.279 --> 00:12:26.189
for something else you're sure to like.

00:12:26.189 --> 00:12:28.269
Thanks for watching and see ya next time.

00:12:28.269 --> 00:12:29.379
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers!

